4a7f-8daa-47bc-a79b-0f20bfa578b4","position":{"commit_sha":"2778ef53ca8753570c7ce3a609eded7a28136a33","position":"1787115361966782001-1ee14a7f-8daa-47bc-a79b-0f20bfa578b4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Completion evidence (C3c cli/commands cutover, Gerrit 1889 — LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1, CI green):\n- 26 LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS rows drained; check_config_ownership.check(REPO_ROOT) reports zero findings for the 22 listed files, no path-glob exception.\n- read-via markers total exactly 2, confined to compact_txn.py (1) + session_id.py (1); every other listed file 0 — proven by held-out tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py (GREEN, teeth confirmed via marker-removal mutant -> 2 RED).\n- Cut-to-seam reads route through owned config.py/_config_sources.py resolvers (incl. new repo_root_or_none, jira-detection, resolve_os_actor); helper signatures unchanged where they read owned resolvers internally.\n- Compose-once timing preserved (none of the 24 cut reads is live-per-operation).\n- docs/env-vars.md regenerated for relocated sources. Full targeted suites green; commit 2831416ac7. file_impact set to the 27 commit files.","timestamp":1787113670666583001}],"created_at":1787095116371265001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"22563b46-544a-445d-917b-e8ce7703e657","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2b5b-b421-dabe-4972"}],"description":"## Implementation status (post-implementation re-review)\nThis slice is IMPLEMENTED and committed (Gerrit 1889, stacked on the C3 chain) in the worktree this plan is re-reviewed against. The 26 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows below were recorded by slice C1 for the cli/commands subsystem and are REMOVED by this slice's commit, so a re-review reading the current `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` correctly sees ZERO rows for these paths and the ownership gate passing. That drained state is the INTENDED END STATE; the enumeration below is the C1 worklist this slice discharges. No further code change is proposed beyond what is committed.\n\n## Context\nSlice C1 (29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 26 below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the cli/commands subsystem (`_cli`, `_commands`) as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows. RP-04 is not done while these sit below the seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab. Each row is still flagged when drained (owner=composition in a non-root file); none already owned.\n\nThe 26 reads: 14 `load_config` + 12 others — `REBAR_ROOT` in `_cli/_init.py` & `_commands/init.py`; `_jira_onboard.py::{JIRA_PROJECT,JIRA_URL,JIRA_USER,os.environ.get}`; `_llm_eval_commands.py::OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`; `bridge_repair.py::USER`; `tracker_maintenance.py::USER`; `compact_txn.py::REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER`; `composer.py::REBAR_DETECTED_BY`; `session_id.py::os.environ.get`. Affected SOURCE files: the 22 read-sites plus `config.py`, `_config_sources.py` (owned resolvers), `config_ownership_exceptions.py` (remove rows).\n\n## Outcome\nEach read gets one treatment and its row is removed. `check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths, no path-glob exception. Behavioral suites stay green; operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except recorded deltas.\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (24 of 26).** A composed-config read is routed through an OWNED `config.py`/`_config_sources.py` resolver instead of an ambient `load_config`/`os.environ` below the seam. The CLI entrypoint composes once and threads the typed value into the below-seam helper (signature changes to RECEIVE it, or the helper reads the owned resolver internally). Timing preserved: a LIVE-per-operation read is cut to a resolver that ALSO reads env live per call. None of these 24 is live-per-operation (CLI resolves each once at entry), per the compose-once proof.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker (capped at 2 reads = 2 marked lines).** A read that is NOT composed config (test-only or harness/protocol env-injection) keeps a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. No other listed read may be marked.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (2 marked lines — the cap)\n1. `compact_txn.py` L186 `REBAR_TEST_COMPACT_RENAME_BARRIER` — test-only failpoint, inert in production. 1 line.\n2. `session_id.py` L57 dynamic `os.environ.get(var)` — harness/protocol env-injection of session identity (`REBAR_SESSION_ID`/`AI_AGENT`/`CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE_SESSION_ID`), read live by `resolve_session_id()`. Shim↔rebar protocol contract, not a config knob. 1 line.\n\n## Cut targets (reuse OWNED resolvers)\n- **14 `load_config`** (`_cli/_audit_commands.py`, `_cli/_jira_onboard.py`, `_commands/{_seam,claim,close_autoresume,compact,compact_trigger,gates,metrics,remote_cert,scratch,verify_authorship,verify_commit,verify_opcert}.py`): CLI composes once at entry and threads the typed `Config`/field into the helper; below-seam `load_config` removed.\n- **2 `REBAR_ROOT`** (`_cli/_init.py`, `_commands/init.py`): duplicate root-discovery that stops at git-toplevel (no cwd fallback) to detect not-found. CUT to a NEW owned `_config_sources.repo_root_or_none(explicit)` (`explicit > REBAR_ROOT > git-toplevel`; None when unresolved), threaded so `_init` maps None→exit 1 and `init` returns None.\n- **5 jira reads** (`_jira_onboard.py` JIRA_URL/USER/PROJECT overlay + `_TOKEN_ENV` detection + presence-gate + `load_config`): CUT to an OWNED jira-detection resolver (file+env, fail-soft ConfigError→env-only, token at credential boundary) returning url/user/project + a `token_present` flag; no env re-read survives or is marked.\n- **`OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`** (`_llm_eval_commands.py`) and **`REBAR_DETECTED_BY`** (`composer.py`): CLI-arg-with-env-default. CUT — the arg still wins; env is the composed default in an OWNED resolver.\n- **2 `USER`** (`bridge_repair._actor`, `tracker_maintenance._actor`): OS-user audit fallback after git identity. CUT to a shared OWNED `resolve_os_actor(tracker)` that TAKES the dir and scopes the SAME `git -C <tracker> config user.email` lookup (git > `$USER` > \"unknown\") — preserves each caller's dir-scoped identity.\n\n## Plan\n1. Reuse/add the OWNED resolvers; cut the 24 composed-config reads through them (thread values into below-seam helpers).\n2. Re-derive changed call sites (Serena `find_referencing_symbols` + a `grep` for the name as a string) and bring into scope, or keep the helper reading an OWNED resolver internally.\n3. Mark the 2 owned-in-place reads; no other markers. Remove the 26 rows. Run `check_config_ownership.py` + suites; keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\nHeld-out `tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts: (i) `check_config_ownership.check(REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding for the 22 listed paths; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries for a listed file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers total exactly 2, confined to `compact_txn.py` (1) + `session_id.py` (1). Compose-once proof: a held-out fixture composes the entrypoint config, mutates each cut env var mid-operation, and asserts the threaded value is UNCHANGED (each cut read is entry-time). Affected suites updated where a signature changed: `tests/unit/{test_audit_*,test_claim_default_assignee,test_compact_*,test_remote_cert,test_verify_commit_ticket,test_verify_opcert*,test_jira_onboard,test_session_id,test_init_*}.py`, `tests/interfaces/{lifecycle,queries}`. Env-setting tests that only set the cut env vars at entry need no change.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored format changes. Cut-to-seam is routing/threading; the 2 marked lines are inline annotations. Rollback = revert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No ambient config/credential read below the seam in the 22 listed files: each is cut-to-seam (24) or one of the 2 owned-in-place reads with a `# read-via:` rationale; any live read cut to a live-per-call resolver.\n- [x] The 26 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows removed; `check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out test incl. marker-total==2 / per-file-placement).\n- [x] The Testing suites pass; operation-snapshot fingerprints / provider-neutral outcomes unchanged except deltas recorded in a comment.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerated env-var registry after relocating reads to owned seams."},{"path":"scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py","reason":"Remove the 26 C3c cli/commands LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS rows as reads are cut to seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_audit_commands.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_init.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/bridge_repair.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/claim.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/gates.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/init.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/metrics.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/scratch.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/session_id.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/tracker_maintenance.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_commit.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_opcert.py","reason":"Cut below-seam ambient config read to the approved owned seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sources.py","reason":"Owned resolvers for the cut cli/commands reads; re-exported from config."},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"Owned resolvers for the cut cli/commands reads; re-exported from config."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_cli_seam_clean_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out seam-clean proof for the cli/commands files."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","075b-1479-dcb7-40ab"],["relates_to","2b5b-b421-dabe-4972"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab","parent_status_uuid":"e8fd17fc-b610-4a09-992d-3a0e7cd7dbc4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9515-ffa1-5272-4310","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.3.c — cli-commands cutover: route below-seam config reads through seams","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cd2970c6-2563-4abe-9cf5-7fb3b3c165bf","c051df6f-0563-47cf-bafc-d31336a9aab0","a0cc886f-30a6-463d-9de8-9fa23a3ee65e","105b0dc8-df13-4a36-b784-9d0dce272b40","75c0e1de-842d-4d4c-9092-21cc0cc76db0","870566d6-7043-4da3-906b-f54a4cfff81c","22563b46-544a-445d-917b-e8ce7703e657","56381195-8db4-4cd8-93ff-40fc8c54ecb5","55347d50-fae1-4ae6-b913-11b3c1e413ea","f536ce42-e490-49ec-b088-974fcb07b8ae","46515442-a07c-4bd1-b4ff-92677c51de3b","b383508e-07bb-4c70-a8d6-bc2a6839cb50","0697ebe4-71e7-4d59-81d1-f7a97737a7e8","e8fd17fc-b610-4a09-992d-3a0e7cd7dbc4","1ee14a7f-8daa-47bc-a79b-0f20bfa578b4"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787118521433804001,"uuid":"85808996-d2c1-4265-83b1-2fe834623ba9"}